A||||59||batboy||The Need For Speed||||1
Z||000000||batboy||11-14-1999||01:21 AM||||I recently bought a computer game called the "Need For Speed III" and have been wasting time playing it lately instead of working on my Fieros. Bad Batboy, bad! You get to race really cool cars, drive on very scenic roads or race tracks, and be chased by speeding ticket writing cops driving hotrod Corvettes. Anyway, I vaguely remember somebody's website that had a downloadable Fiero computer car file for the original "Need For Speed" game. Does anyone know what that site URL was or whether a Fiero file is available for this version 3 game? I feel the need...the need for speed! I'd love to have my own custom made Batmobile computer car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||11-14-1999||02:23 AM||||I found the site, but the link was broken and the guy never replied to my email.<P>so, since I couldn't download one.. what I did was alter the model for the F355, changed the performance, and made a new skin for it. not perfect, but it was acceptable. Now I just drive the Porsche 911 (another car I downloaded) or the Corvette.<P>I'm gonna be getting NFS4 sometime soon, it's just like NFS3 but with more realistic physics as well as damage..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||11-14-1999||06:49 AM|||| <A HREF="http://freehosting2.at.webjump.com/39dfdc050/fi/fieros-webjump/86fierogt.zip" TARGET=_blank>http://freehosting2.at.webjump.com/39dfdc050/fi/fieros-webjump/86fierogt.zip</A> . Here you can download a Fiero for NFSIII (from  <A HREF="http://fieros.webjump.com" TARGET=_blank>http://fieros.webjump.com</A> . I haven't tested it since I don't have NFSIII.<P>I'm a huge racingsim fan, but I mostly play Formula 1 Racing Simulation or Monaco Grand Prix Racing Simulation. I made small cockpit type thingy for my Logitech Force Feedback Wheel which I can attach to an old chair. Hooked my PC to a 32" widescreen tv too! Great setup! Haven't raced an online race yet. Maybe some people here have these racing sims too and we can do a race sometime!<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000003||batboy||11-14-1999||12:39 PM||||Cliff, you got me all excited about the thought of downloading that NFS3 Fiero file, but now I can't get the link to work. You think it's a temporary server problem?<P>Darklord, is this the same site you were thinking of? How hard is it to modify the code for the cars. Once I get a good Fiero file, I'd like to tweak it to reflect the color of my car, set it up with V8 power, and add the suspension mods I've done.<P>I've never played a racing game online with others in head to head competition. Sounds like fun! Years ago I had Test Drive 3, then I got the first Need For Speed (both of which are antique DOS games).<P>Remember when we thought DOS games were neat? You know, before Pentium CPUs, high speed CD-ROMs, 3-D video cards, 17 inch monitors, and awesome computer sound systems. Oh no! Flash back! I'm remembering ancient history now...my first "real" computer was a Commodore 64 with a cassette tape player drive for file storage. Times have sure changed, huh?||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||11-14-1999||12:48 PM||||That might have been the site, I don't really remember.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>but the filename sounds right. I'll see if I still have the files for the car I modified, only problem is it's a spyder, so if you want it to look like it has a roof you gotta set the car's color to black, no reflections.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>and it already handles like a porsche, with as close to slightly modified V6 performance as I can get.||||reg||1
