Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||11-14-1999||03:04 PM||||I checked the link and it works. I've taken the liberty of downloading it to my server:  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86fierogt.zip" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86fierogt.zip</A> . Like I said, I haven't tested it so I have no idea what's actually in this zip file. I also don't really know if I'm violating some copyright here, so I will only temporarily have it on my server - grab it while it's there...||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||11-14-1999||04:45 PM||||Cliff, thanks for the effort, but that file you put on your server is invalid. A valid file is 815K in size. I finally got one of those links (the second one) to work and it took me several attempts to download the whole file. Everytime I tried to multi-task, the download would bomb off. Also, that website you listed has lots of other nice Fiero links and other great stuff to see.<P>Anyway, I finally got it working and have played the game once now. WOW! It is so cool to be racing a Fiero in the game. I think it's so neat to see that familar Fiero gauge cluster when you're playing. I had it up to 150 mph on a long straight before I crashed and ended upsidedown. I still ended up in 5th place out of 8 cars on my first attempt even after recovering from my crash. Are these cars tough or what? I not only survived a 150 mph accident, but got the Fiero back into the race in seconds. This 86 GT model uses a 3800 supercharged engine that put out 240 hp. Wow again! Too bad it's not a notchback.<P>This guy actually modified the file from another person. I went to the original designer's website, but can't get the car to download at all. His site is:<BR>  <A HREF="http://www3.sympatico.ca/matjasko/fiero/pics/nfs3/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www3.sympatico.ca/matjasko/fiero/pics/nfs3/index.html</A> ||||reg||1
