Z||000011||ggarsk||11-14-1999||05:39 PM||||Thanks Cliff,I had no trouble downloading the file. I'll have to check it out tomorrow after work. I had forgot all about that till batboy brought it up.||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||11-14-1999||07:18 PM||||I tried the Fiero.. handling isn't quite what I'm used to with the Porsche 911 and the Corvette.. but the acceleration is awesome. Put a power steering module in that car, and some expensive suspension upgrades, and it'd be incredible.. as it is now it's pretty cool, I'll need to practice driving with it. Got it up to 243kph and didn't crash too many times the first time driving tho.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||batboy||11-14-1999||09:04 PM||||I've played with my Fiero in the game some more too. Acceleration is awesome, but being light weight, I notice that I have more "air time" than any of the other cars. I even landed on top of another car once when I took a "Dukes of Hazard" jump. Later, I got into a spectacular 4 car pile up, rolled it, landed back on my wheels pointed in the right direction, so I floored it and kept racing.<P>I tweaked the car settings around a little. Put a little higher gear in it for more top speed, made the steering quicker, and firmed up the suspension. Now I'm driving more agressively, throwing the car around, tapping the brakes for a second to swing the rear out on sharp curves, etc. The Fiero handles more predictably under these extreme conditions then most of the other cars in the game. I love it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Standard||11-15-1999||03:01 AM||||I just got my hands on NFS3 and when I'm not on this site I've been playing that!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I've been a fan of the NFS series ever since the first one came out.  The one thing I don't like about NFS3 is they don't have the movies of cars in the showcases.  Oh well.  Very nice game otherwise.  Now I've just gotta get that Fiero model!||||reg||14
Z||000015||Cliff Pennock||11-15-1999||03:47 AM||||Okay, y'all convinced me! NFS3 has been in the bargain bin here for quite some time, but I had never picked it up. I loved NFS2 but somehow never got around buying NFS3. I'll get it today.<P>PS: Does it have internet play? It would be great if we could organize an online Fiero-only internet race (or even a small tournament?).||||reg||6
