Z||000018||Cliff Pennock||11-15-1999||04:44 PM||||Hmmmm, finally got NFS3 running (after three hours of installing, uninstalling, reinstalling, patch-installing, uninstalling, etc..), the game just wouldn't run the first 6 installs.<P>First impression was that the graphics are very jerky. 550Mhz PC, 128Mb Ram and a Voodoo3/3000 ought to be enough you would think... (all of my other games including NFS2 run super smooth, even at 1024x768)<P>Anyway, tried the Fiero. Hmmmm. That is <B>not</B> a Fiero dashboard. Drove it. What the... 165mph! Yeah, in my dreams!<P>Don't get me wrong, I like the <B>idea</B> being able to drive a Fiero in the game and I sure appreciate the effort made by those involved, but I was a bit disappointed because although it looked somewhat similar to a Fiero, it didn't give me the feeling at all of <B>being</B> in a Fiero... Did I do something wrong installing the car? I just created a directory ".../CarData/Fier", unzipped the file there and chose Fiero GT in the game...||||reg||9
Z||000019||Formula||11-15-1999||05:54 PM||||mine runs smooth on a 200mhz pc with 80 mbs ram and a voodoo card. Did you play with the resolution? the fiero did seem a bit fast but I opened the txt file and it gave top spped specs, torque curve, etc..... I think that it would be easy to slow it down like a real fiero. Instead of the dash, I always use the behind the car view. It looks sooooooo much like a real fiero! I just pretend its batboys fiero I'm driving!!!||||reg||1
Z||000020||four50four||11-15-1999||06:00 PM||||man, i gotta get me this game! what's it worth??||||reg||2
Z||000021||batboy||11-15-1999||06:08 PM||||Cliff, I wonder if there's some conflict or problem with your game. Mine loaded first time and runs smooth as silk. I'm running 450 MHz, 128 meg of ram, and a Voodoo II card. But then I'm running my game at 800 X 600 resolution. Hope you get it figured out.<P>Just thought of something, what speed of CD-ROM do you have, before I got my fast Kenwood Multi-beam unit, some graphic intensive games would act a little jerky if it was waiting for the CD-ROM to catch up.<P>Well...my NFS3 Fiero dash looks fairly authentic, except for the round temp and fuel gauge. The shape of the dash pod looked real to me and the tach and speedo look ok. Everything is not perfect, but hey, it's just a game. To me it does feel a lot like being in a Fiero.<P>I didn't care for the bra either and all three of my cars are notchbacks, but I like having a Fiero in the game. Also, according to the instructions, multi-player internet play should be possible. I'd better do a bunch more practicing before I compete with real people. This rookie is still crashing a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000022||DaRkLoRD||11-15-1999||07:07 PM||||runs great on my system. P2-400, 64mb SDRAM, 8mb AGP ATI Xpert@Play video card, 32x cdrom.<BR>I'm running it at 24-bit color, 800 x 600.<P>That is the stock F355 interior from the game. hasn't been modified at all, so unless you have the PISA dash and the replica gauges, your Fiero isn't gonna look like that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>(unless I screwed up the install.. hehe)<P>four50four: it's under $50 cdn in Ontario. NFS4 is about the same price, and has all the same tracks, plus some new ones.. New cars as well. A friend has it, and we spent one night seeing how could make the coolest crash with the McLaren F1.. we had a Porsche 911 backfiring and trailing smoke.. fun.<P>Batboy: I've been playing NFS3 for about 7 months, and I still crash a lot.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||Cliff Pennock||11-15-1999||07:24 PM||||I got it for US$20 from the bargain bin. I think I know why it's running like sh*t. This is the European version and <B>none</B> of the patches made available for this game will work on the European version (besides the Voodoo3 screen driver). So I guess I'm stuck with the original OOTB version...<P>What <B>really</B> bugs me (to say it politely) is that the box has the 3DFx logo on it, while it <B>doesn't</B> support 3DFx cards OOTB. The 3DFx logo can only be used by games that explicitly use the native 3DFx (Glide) drivers. And it doesn't.<P>*SIGH*... This is the 6th game out of 7 I bought these past months that doesn't work without heavy patching...||||reg||1
Z||000024||batboy||11-15-1999||09:33 PM||||Oops, boy is my face red. Darklord's right about the dash being the same as the F-355, except they tried to put ralley gauges on it. I should of known better than to doubt Cliff. Sorry, I guess I was so excited about racing the Fiero I didn't look all that close at the dash. Hard to do when you're taking a curve at triple digit speeds, even in a game.<P>Since the new NFS is out at $45 (US dollars) they had the version 3 game marked down to $20 where I bought mine. I'm half tempted to buy another game and ship it to Cliff so he could have a US version that supports the Voodoo and don't need all the blankity-blank patches.<P>Formula, as long as you're JUST pretending to be driving my beloved Batmobile, I'll let you dream...LOL. You mentioned wanting to slow it down so it was more like a real Fiero, well it's modeled after a 3800 supercharged engine swap that puts out 240 HP. There are real Fieros with that conversion. Actually, that's more HP than my tired ol' 350 V8 that's currently in the Batmobile.<P>Crazy!!! I didn't think I'd get any response from this topic, except maybe a website URL, if I was lucky. You guys amaze me sometimes, you're as batty as me.||||reg||1
