Z||000028||Standard||11-16-1999||02:04 AM||||I'm running on a K6-300 w/ 64mb ram and a Voodoo Banshee and the game runs smooooth in 800x600... but I also got that auto-patcher and let it get all the patches.  It would be possible to make a notchback model, and edit the values to make it more realistic, but it's pretty complicate.  I downloaded a program called Car-Cad that lets you edit the models, and one called VivWizard that'll let you edit the data.. but I've never been good with that 3d stuff and I don't completly understand some of the data in the .viv files..they have brake curves, gas curves, turn modifiers, so many things you can fool with.  I got the files at <A HREF="http://www.nfscheats.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nfscheats.com</A>   pretty cool site.<BR>another good place is <A HREF="http://nfscentral.mgon.com" TARGET=_blank>http://nfscentral.mgon.com</A>   lots of cars to download there.  Get the Mclaren F1... can you say 222mph top speed? crazy fast car..||||reg||6
