Z||000060||chris6878||11-24-1999||10:17 PM||||You play need for speed via the net by choosing the "connect players" option...<P> u then use the "Network (tcp)" to connect players using your IP address...   the person hosting the game will have to tell the other players their ip # and then they can join the game.<P>You can go to <A HREF="http://www.heat.net" TARGET=_blank>www.heat.net</A>  to use the "network (ipx)" option to play using the internet...  you have to download the heat software which creates a virtual network to play by...   or if you and the other players are on the same network, then all u need to do is host a game and the others will be able to see and join the game....   <P>I hope i havent confused anyone.....    have fun racing...     i have tuned up my fiero on nfs3 and it tops at 196 mph so far...  later....<P>chris||||reg||3
